## Conclusion
* The external prior (clpeak MI50 @1725MHz: float 766 / float2 757 / float4 741 GB/s)
  UNDERSTATES this card's achievable pure-read bandwidth by 7-21%. It is not used.
* Two independent implementations agree the real number is in the 820-930 GB/s band:
    - 928 GB/s  hand-written Triton read-stream (the class of kernel #20 will be)
    - 821 GB/s  torch.sum reduction (a library kernel, less optimally vectorised)
* Floor used for every #20 judgement = 821 GB/s (the conservative one, i.e. the number
  that does NOT flatter the case for writing the kernel). 928 is recorded as the
  measured pure-read ceiling.
* Consequence for the section 2 VALU budget: at 821 GB/s the budget is
  6.62e12 / (821e9/0.5) = 4.03 op/weight against 3.85 needed with the zp hoist
  -> headroom ~4.6%, not the ~13% an external review derived from 760 GB/s.
  At 928 GB/s the budget falls to 3.56 -> the kernel would be VALU-bound, not
  bandwidth-bound. Either way #20 lives or dies on measured per-shape efficiency
  (Task 4), not on distance to a bandwidth floor.
